      <p>The chosen headline, number <span id="best-headline">1</span></p>

      <h2>BAB: before, after, bridge</h2>
      <div id="bab">
        <p class="part" data-part="before"><span class="tag">Before:</span> You keep putting this off because it isn’t clear where to start.</p>
        <p class="part" data-part="after"><span class="tag">After:</span> You know the order of work, the time and the price, and you can get on with other things.</p>
        <p class="part" data-part="bridge"><span class="tag">Bridge:</span> {{mainAction.label}}</p>
      </div>

      <h2>4 Ps for a page</h2>
      <div id="four-p">
        <p class="part" data-part="picture"><span class="tag">Picture:</span> You come to the page with a question and see at once what to do.</p>
        <p class="part" data-part="promise"><span class="tag">Promise:</span> We name the order of work, the time and the price before work starts.</p>
        <p class="part" data-part="prove"><span class="tag">Prove:</span> {{#each proofs}}{{title}}. {{/each}}All of it can be checked against the documents.</p>
        <p class="part" data-part="push"><span class="tag">Push:</span> {{mainAction.label}}</p>
      </div>

      <h2>QUEST for an email</h2>
      <div id="quest">
        <p class="part" data-part="qualify"><span class="tag">Qualify:</span> This email is for people facing this kind of task for the first time who want to understand the order of work.</p>
        <p class="part" data-part="understand"><span class="tag">Understand:</span> We know that in matters like these it is hard to find your way without preparation.</p>
        <p class="part" data-part="educate"><span class="tag">Educate:</span> Here are three steps: go through your situation, name the time and the price, do the work.</p>
        <p class="part" data-part="stimulate"><span class="tag">Stimulate:</span> The terms are known in advance, and the result can be checked against the documents.</p>
        <p class="part" data-part="transition"><span class="tag">Transition:</span> {{mainAction.label}}</p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </body>
</html>
`
